# Machine registry: prod machines only.
# Copy to etc/machines.ini (git-ignored; commit it only in a private fork) and
# fill in your entries — or keep it in a private config repo and inject it via
# .private-source (see doc/system/private-config.md). `pf-deploy.sh` (the
# framework CLI wrapped by bin/deploy.sh) and `gen-reuter` read the [prod]
# roster; the dev-machine `DBUSER` mapping now lives in etc/team.ini (see
# etc/team.ini.template), not here.
#
# [prod] prod deploy targets. Each key is the server's ZeroTier IP (the same
#        address `pf-deploy.sh` uses for SSH). The value is a comma-separated
#        list of `tag[:name]` tokens:
#          named tag   `db:simo`  -> a `db` resource named `simo`
#          bare tag    `worker`   -> boolean flag (install cron on this host)
#        `db` (named) and `worker` (bare) are the framework's built-in tags:
#        a `db:<name>` token provisions a MariaDB instance + `gen-reuter`
#        connectivity; `worker` installs the `cron-manifest` output (cron
#        jobs) on every deploy. Every other tag is consumer-owned:
#          `web`     restore Apache www-data traversal on the repo dir
#        A host with a `db:<name>` token is a database host; a bare `worker`
#        token adds cron install on that host; an empty value is a code-only
#        server (it deploys the codebase but runs no tagged step).
#
#        Constraint: a named token may appear on exactly ONE server
#        (`db:simo` and `web` are independent). Bare flags carry no name,
#        hence no uniqueness constraint. A server may host no database
#        (code-only), one database, or several databases in its MariaDB
#        instance.

[prod]
# 10.147.x.10=db:simo, db:analytics, web, worker
